Tuesday
Today we had District Council Meeting, and our district leader had us start
off with a game of speed to decide the order we'd do something, since we
were in the church gym for the meeting. By the way, the order literally did
not matter for what we were doing =F0=9F=98=82 our DL just really likes bas=
ketball
lol. Afterwards Elder Sonomura and I both gave an individual training,
which went well. I basically hid a bunch of papers around the gym and had
people try to find them all to teach a lesson lol. Right after that, Elder
Sonomura and I went and God sushi with a recently fairly new member. It was
very good, and I got to try a pretty big variety of sushi. I had (I think)
salmon, tuna, squid, octopus, eel, shrimp and I think one other. Was mostly
pretty tasty Lol. Today we also officially moved to Hirakata even though it
isn't even the end of the transfer lol. The apartment we are using used to
be the Pace's, and literally everything is brand new =F0=9F=98=82 its super=
 nice.
Only drawback is, we are still attending like every activity in Ibaraki and
its almost an hour bike ride =F0=9F=98=B5 Its fine but really annoying not =
having a
specific place we are staying all the time. I wrote down that we talked to
two ladies, but I genuinely can't remember when or what it was about =F0=9F=
=98=82 All
around good day.

Wednesday
For lunch Elder Sonomura and I got some soumen (I think) and it was
badically cold buckwheat noodles that you dip into a broth to eat. Was very
tasty. We also did a Jkaiwa meeting with a dude named Guzman, from America.
At the end when we shared our usual spiritual message, he took it super
well; he prayed for us and is going to read the intro to the Book of
Mormon. Super excited to hear how it goes! Today we did some streeting with
now Elder Ikawa (used to be Toku san, he leaves for America in a week) and
also a bunch of housing. It was pretty good, and fun to see how a native
Japanese speaker approaches those with the same native language. Today we
also had Eikaiwa, which didn't go much differently than usual; Elder Berg
and I taught the advanced class, but we mostly just had a normal English
conversation the whole time rather than doing specific activities.

Thursday
Today we stopped (I say stopped by pretty lightly, it was very far out of
the way lol) by the police station to pick up Elder Sonomuras's lost and
found wallet lol. Afterwards we spent about 4 or 5 hours with Mai and a
couple ward members at Round One, an arcade, sports, and bowling center.
the Zl's didn't seem to mind us going and Elder Sonomura didn't say
anything about it, but the whole time I was thinking: how is this
missionary work?? =F0=9F=98=82 I mean we are definitely strengthening our
relationship with our friends, and we had an awesome spiritual lesson at
the end, but like still bro =F0=9F=98=82 Later we had Basketball night as u=
sually, in
which I played with a few people on the =E2=80=9Ccasual play=E2=80=9D side =
of the gym lol.
Before we actually started the basketball stuff, we had a Jkaiwa Lesson
which went awesome! we even had our friend pray at the end of class for the
first time, it was great! High hopes for this man =F0=9F=98=81

Friday
Today we had to get our bikes over to the Hirakata Apartment, And I carried
half of my laundry on my back for the whole hour bike ride =F0=9F=92=80 It =
was tough,
but wasn't like as super miserable as it might sound. Today we did more
streeting with Ikawa =E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 and it was super fun. Love this guy=
 =F0=9F=94=A5 When we were
finished streeting, we met up with Moriguchi san in person, which was
awesome! I imagined in my head on the way that she might be like super
short for some reason, and she indeed was =F0=9F=98=82 Funny coincidence lo=
l. We had
a great message with her, even if I was getting absolutely demolished by
mosquitos. When I got home I had 6 bites on just my left ankle =F0=9F=98=A2=
 While we
were getting back from meeting Moriguchi san, I actually ran into my cousin
from America =F0=9F=98=82 She was visiting Japan for like a week or somethi=
ng and
unfortunately wasn't visiting any of the areas that I was going to be in.
EXCEPT we had to suddenly move to Hirakata and we miraculously bumped into
each other; it was not statistically possible, but God has his ways I
suppose =F0=9F=98=81 Was super fun to talk to her for even a few minutes lo=
l. When we
parted ways (probably for real that time lol) we met some guy on the bus
ride home and he talked to us about some super healthy tofu for like an
hour lol. There was the Youth Gathering as well, in which we taught Nao and
Mai, it was great! They are slowly but surely progressing.

Saturday
Soran dance at a festival with kids
Today we had a sports meeting with the YSA for two hours (kind of a bunch
of random competitions; throwing bean bags, balloon relay race, that sort
of thing. Immediately after (like an hour after I guess) we had our sports
night for another 2 hours lol. It was very fun, played some great
volleyball, but there's not a whole lot to say about it lol.

Sunday
Today we had our usual sacrament meeting, which was awesome. Kind of
random, but there's a foreigner named Zach who goes to the ward, and after
church he had Like 3 people I noticed just rubbing his belly =F0=9F=98=82=
=F0=9F=98=82 he isn't
a big dude or anything either, but everyone thinks Hes like super sift =F0=
=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=82
so weird bro. After church we went and visited a newly built shrine, as
well as a big dam, with Toyama san. It was super cool. When we finished
getting down the stairs from the top of the dam, we got to talk to some
Japanese Cub Scout Leaders, which was so fun. When I told them I was an
Eagle scout they called me their senpai =F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=82 basically =
upperclassmen lol.
They were super friendly though! Afterwards, we met up with a new member at
a college nearby and talk with him in English for around an hour. His name
is Rui, and he's so cool; he speaks super natural English and is super nice
and loves talking to the missionaries! Only problem is he doesn't like
going to church because he thinks that Japanese members are super weird. He
literally said they were like another race =F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=82 (hate t=
o break it to you
dude, you're also a Japanese member) (he got baptized while visiting
America for a year btw) Later we went to the Ikawas to say goodbye to Ikawa
=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 and teach a lesson to his friend Ayane. It was sad to sa=
y goodbye, but
he's going to serve his mission in Seattle, so i'm sure it'll go well!! On
the way home we rode the monorail again, which I think is just the coolest
thing, and it's probably just normal for everyone else Riding it =F0=9F=98=
=82

P-day
Today we went to Kyoto. First thing we did was get some Ramen (mine was
very spicy). Afterwards we went to a Pok=C3=A9mon store, and then the Ninte=
ndo
store. It was pretty fun, but I was a bit bummed I didn't get a great
chance to take many pictures lol. We were just kind of inside looking at
stuff the whole time =F0=9F=98=82 Still fun though. It is also pretty dang =
far from
Ibaraki and Hirakata, So like half of the day was probably traveling. I
also got a haircut with Elder Sonomura, but that's about it Lol.

Love you guys!!!! You are all so precious to me!!
-=E3=82=AD=E3=83=AA=E3=82=A2=E3=83=B3=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81

Spiritual thought!!!!!!
This is my favorite scripture, and if you can I'd Love if you could send me
yours sometime this week, I'd love to learn more about what you guys enjoy
from the Gospel as well =F0=9F=91=8D=F0=9F=91=8D
Alma 36:22
22 Yea, methought I saw, even as our father Lehi saw, God sitting upon his
throne, surrounded with numberless concourses of angels, in the attitude of
singing and praising their God; yea, and my soul did long to be there.

